.TH PAGE 1
.SH NAME
page \- show documents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wm/page
[
.B -r
.I quarters
]
[
.B -w
|
.B -f
|
.B -z
.I percent
]
[
.I file ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Page
shows documents: PDF files, images, Markdown, Mermaid diagrams and
HTML, each by the engine for its kind
(see
.IR docengine (2)),
in the view Xenith's windows use
.RI ( sheetview (2)):
a column of its pages, fitted to the window's width (a PDF) or a
whole page in view (a picture), scrolled smoothly from page to page.
.PP
The files named are one document: paging on past a file's last page
goes to the next file's first, and back.  Only the file shown is held
open.  With no file named,
.I page
reads the document from its standard input.
.PP
.B -r
turns the pages
.I quarters
quarter turns clockwise;
.B -w
fits the width,
.B -f
a whole page,
.B -z
sets the scale to
.I percent
of the pages' size.
.PP
Button 1 drags the pages in both directions; the wheel scrolls them.
As in Plan 9's
.IR page ,
button 2 raises a menu of operations: the next and previous page, zoom
in and out, fit width or page, turn right or left,
.BR find... ,
.BR "go to page..." ,
.B "write page..."
(the page shown, at the scale shown, as an image file, see
.IR image (6)),
and
.BR exit .
Button 3 raises a menu of the pages to choose from: those near the one
shown (marked
.BR * ),
the first and the last, and, with several files, the files.
A status line names the file, the page and the scale.
.PP
Keys:
.TF "Page Down"
.TP
space, Page Down
a screen on (into the next file at a file's end)
.TP
backspace, Page Up
a screen back
.TP
Down, Up
scroll
.TP
.BR n ", Right"
the next page
.TP
.BR p ", Left"
the previous page
.TP
Home, End
the first file's first page, the last file's last
.TP
.BR + ", " -
zoom in, out
.TP
.BR w ", " f
fit the width, a whole page
.TP
.BR r ", " R
turn right, left
.TP
.B /
find
.TP
.B g
go to a page
.TP
.B W
write the page shown as an image
.TP
.B q
quit
.PD
.PP
A page is painted at the scale shown, off the window's thread, and
kept while it is in view or the next the way the pages last moved;
until it is ready the last painting is shown scaled.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/wm/page.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR docengine (2),
.IR sheetview (2),
.IR wm (1)
